    "training_evaluation": "Change only NEGATIVES from 128 to 512, preserving Histories.__getitem__(self, index), uniform training-only sampling, rejection of items in the user's full training history, duplicate-negative behavior, and sharing each history's negatives across supervised transitions. Preserve ConvRec.training_loss(seq, pos, neg), all existing variable names and function signatures: its existing einsum and concatenation will create 513-class logits with the positive at class zero, retaining padding masks, unreduced cross-entropy, recency weights with half-life 10, and per-history normalization; let the existing check_model exercise the increased negative dimension. Explicitly keep unchanged the ConvRec backbone, relative-distance attention, jointly learned item bias, dimensions, dropout, history length, prefix augmentation, batch size, optimizer, learning-rate schedule, steps, SASREC_EPOCHS default 200, early stopping, single-checkpoint selection, deterministic worker seeding, and runtime/deadline allocation. Preserve preprocessing seed 0, training seed 42, evaluation seed 42, supplied splits, all four categories and routing, DATA_DIR=os.environ['GAGC_DATA_DIR'], trial-local artifacts, single-GPU execution, and write_predict_script loading exactly one newly trained selected checkpoint per category with identical validation/inference scoring; introduce no ensembles, auxiliary fitted scorers, checkpoint reuse, external data, hidden-test access, or evaluator changes. Compare pinned-host macro validation HR@10 against 0.5312 using 200 users per category and 99 unique negatives, inspect category regressions and recorded runtime/GPU memory within the shared 43,200 GPU-second budget, and treat the proposed 0.005–0.015 gain as an unmeasured hypothesis."
